{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpnU4SApAHFivvvS6dQh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It depends on the version. In Vitest 5 and later, `-t` / `testNamePattern` matches against the full test name with `>` between the nested `describe` names and the test name, for example `outer > inner > my test`. The v5.0.0 release notes list this as a breaking change: \"Use `>` as separator in `-t`\" (PR #10686). In Vitest 4 and earlier, the names are joined with spaces, for example `outer inner my test`. If you upgrade, any `-t` regex that spans suite and test names needs to change to the new separator.\n\nSources:\n- [Vitest v5.0.0 release notes](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/releases/tag/v5.0.0)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":381,"cache_read_input_tokens":5392,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":381},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69f9f2a6-5200-48ea-9232-8d2688d08a50","uuid":"3625dec8-e17f-43c7-bbf2-557b230d07a9","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:39:38.838Z","request_id":"req_011CfpnU49odfUP6KMQBsd3H"}
